markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Synchronous vs. Asynchronous

<img src="https://images.code.org/6f13673a0ca38964117b3ad1e8261040-image-1771342723588.png" alt="cartoon image of chef flipping a pancake" width="275px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 0 0px 20px;">

#### In real programs, some tasks happen immediately, while others take time.

#### The question is not whether waiting happens.  
#### The real question is: **What does the program do while it waits?**

#### In this activity, we’ll compare two patterns:
- ####  **Synchronous (blocking):** Tasks happen one at a time, in order.
- ####  **Asynchronous (non-blocking):** Some tasks are scheduled to finish later, allowing other work to continue.


<div style="clear:both;"></div>


---

